1
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:19,450
Nagi's miraculous goal equalizes the score!!

2
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,390
Look at the excitement filling the stadium!!

3
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,540
Who on earth is this Nagi...?

4
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:30,880
Could the Blue Lock project actually be... succeeding...?

5
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:37,090
It's anyone's guess who the hero of this match will be now!!

6
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:45,040
...How embarrassing.

7
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,480
Nagi.

8
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:50,840
...Damn.

9
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,360
...You missed your chance to be the hero.

10
00:00:53,590 --> 00:00:55,440
This is just the beginning!

11
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:58,650
...What an irritating goal.

12
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:02,290
...This works...! We can do this.

13
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,370
...We can reach... the world stage!

14
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:45,360
Hooray! We equalized!

15
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:49,540
But why did our attack suddenly become effective, I wonder...?

16
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,310
...We were struggling so much just a moment ago.

17
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,980
...Don't let the goal itself consume all your thoughts, Assistant.

18
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,360
...The key to the goal lies in what preceded it.

19
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,510
In what preceded it...?

20
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,570
...I mean the start of the attack that led to the goal.

21
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:09,660
The origin of that goal was Itoshi Rin's improvisation.

22
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:13,730
Didn't I tell you before that our players are strong on the real stage?

23
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:18,920
...They're armed with the improvisation they've honed throughout the entire Blue Lock selection.

24
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:22,800
Do you mean things like that so-called chemical reaction?

25
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,100
...Yes... that's also a form of improvisation.

26
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:37,590
...When one pursues a goal, things rarely go exactly as planned.

27
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:47,370
The truths written in textbooks or guidebooks are nothing but empty theories in the face of the reality of the battlefield.

28
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:51,090
...When the plan made fails,

29
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:59,680
...ordinary people panic and try to find a reason for the failure to calm themselves down.

30
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:02,960
...That's the mindset of losers.

31
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:06,100
What is our goal in this match, Anri-chan?

32
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:10,430
Well... to win, of course!

33
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:11,770
Correct.

34
00:04:11,770 --> 00:04:16,470
...Winners never lose sight of their goals; they simply accept this new challenge.

35
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:25,150
...As long as we don't forget our goal even if our plan fails,

36
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:28,820
I'll never give up! Let's go to Onigashima!

37
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:32,740
...this situation becomes a new challenge.

38
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:36,960
...That's... the mindset needed for improvisation.

39
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:40,920
...Blue Lock has no need for ordinary people who wait for instructions.

40
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:47,150
...We want egoists who can find challenges on their own!

41
00:04:47,150 --> 00:04:51,180
...And the one who did that before anyone else was Itoshi Rin.

42
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:54,140
...Then Isagi Yoichi responded to that.

43
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:59,280
...Isagi Yoichi is essential for awakening Itoshi Rin, just as I expected.

44
00:05:00,850 --> 00:05:02,580
Let's go and score the second one!

45
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:03,310
Right!

46
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:06,650
...Our goal just now.

47
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:09,570
...I wouldn't have been surprised no matter which of them scored.

48
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:13,070
...The shooting ability of all three of them is extremely high.

49
00:05:13,710 --> 00:05:17,130
...But that wouldn't have happened if we hadn't disrupted their formation.

50
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:20,960
...That was the reason we created situations where we could use our weapons just as we trained.

51
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:25,130
...And the one who paved the way for us to do that was undoubtedly Rin.

52
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:29,850
...Just watch me.

53
00:05:30,450 --> 00:05:34,430
...Those words helped me focus on linking up with Rin's play.

54
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,250
...Rin gave me a new challenge.

55
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,470
...Rin!

56
00:05:41,870 --> 00:05:43,610
...Your shot was close.

57
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:47,160
...But you led the attack well; I'm sure you'll score next ti-

58
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:50,140
Shut up! Are you trying to provoke me?

59
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:52,280
Nothing has value except the goal!

60
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:55,460
...But thanks to what you did, we were able to sco-

61
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:56,670
So what?

62
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,700
Weren't you trying to score yourself too?

63
00:06:00,290 --> 00:06:03,750
...You were stuck to me like goldfish poop when we were in midfield.

64
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:07,590
But as soon as we got close to the penalty area, you separated from me, following your egoism, trying to score.

65
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:10,050
Is there a problem with that...?

66
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:11,950
No, it was brilliant.

67
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:15,760
...We both use and consume each other for our own goals.

68
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:20,900
Isn't this twisted relationship... the best for both of us...?

69
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:22,940
...Yeah.

70
00:06:26,410 --> 00:06:30,240
...I see... this relationship between us is what produces our unpredictable movements.

71
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:34,090
...Right now, we... pose a threat to them!

72
00:06:35,890 --> 00:06:38,360
...Don't relax...! Just fight.

73
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:41,730
For your own goal, and nothing else!

74
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,980
Fifteen minutes left until the end of the first half!

75
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:48,400
Who would have expected such a development in the match?

76
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,430
You're right... I'm getting goosebumps from excitement!

77
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:53,710
And now the match resumes with a score of 1-1!

78
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:57,140
Hey, you!

79
00:06:57,950 --> 00:07:00,200
Half of the first half has already passed.

80
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,680
You haven't even greeted your brother after a long absence, you filthy brother.

81
00:07:06,350 --> 00:07:09,580
This isn't a match to show off your abilities!

82
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:12,940
It's the match where I surpass you!!!

83
00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:14,820
Here it is!

84
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,750
Pass to me, Sae-kun!

85
00:07:19,750 --> 00:07:20,830
I'll support you, Rin!

86
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,250
Don't you dare interfere, Isagi!

87
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,450
Get lost, you outsiders!

88
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:27,150
This is a sibling quarrel!

89
00:07:28,770 --> 00:07:30,920
A sibling quarrel on such a big stage?

90
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:33,510
Are you monopolizing the game for yourselves...?

91
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:39,430
...How skilled...! He masterfully used his shoulder to protect the ball against Rin's pressure.

92
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,560
What incredible ball keeping and turning!

93
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,520
...No.

94
00:07:43,090 --> 00:07:45,730
Rin read that and kept up with him.

95
00:07:50,390 --> 00:07:53,940
...If you remain fixated on being my little brother,

96
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:01,290
you'll never surpass me... as long as I live.

97
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,630
...A crossover elastico...?

98
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:09,130
He dribbled past him!!! Itoshi Sae has broken through the midfield!

99
00:08:09,130 --> 00:08:10,810
Sae-kun is amazing!!

100
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:15,420
The winner of the first round of the sibling showdown is the older brother!

101
00:08:16,310 --> 00:08:18,640
Did you lose, you lower-eyelash bastard...?

102
00:08:18,930 --> 00:08:19,890
Here they come!

103
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,600
The opponent is rushing at us with numerical intensity!

104
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:26,730
Stay alert in the defensive line, Niko boy!

105
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:27,560
Right!

106
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,350
...Niko Ikki.

107
00:08:31,350 --> 00:08:37,230
Do you know why I chose you as a starting center back despite your average height and speed?

108
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,570
Because of my field of vision...?

109
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:40,860
Correct.

110
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:50,540
Your extraordinary ability to accurately read the state of the field is what makes you the watchtower of Blue Lock!

111
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:58,130
...Track every player trying to link up with Itoshi Sae!

112
00:08:58,130 --> 00:09:02,770
...And among those opening up space to receive his pass,

113
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:07,060
...find the most dangerous one... and stop him!

114
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:14,700
...No, wait... this pass has backspin, which will make it easy to control.

115
00:09:15,090 --> 00:09:17,120
...And even if I sprint at full speed,

116
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,610
...I'll still be half a step behind.

117
00:09:20,590 --> 00:09:22,740
This... is a trap!

118
00:09:23,070 --> 00:09:25,960
...They're trying to draw me out to break down our formation.

119
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,340
...Then they'll easily break through our defense with a single touch.

120
00:09:28,340 --> 00:09:31,210
...This is a high-level trap set by Itoshi Sae!

121
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:34,750
...And if I fall for it... it's over!

122
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,130
How naive you are, genius.

123
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:43,010
...I'll pretend to have fallen into your trap.

124
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,930
...Then, half a step before...

125
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:46,100
...I'll stop.

126
00:09:47,230 --> 00:09:50,440
...And then the ball will be slightly higher than his control point.

127
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:53,060
And all I have to do is clear it!

128
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:54,650
Nice, Niko!

129
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:55,930
Loose ball!

130
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,190
Alright, you bunch of lunatics!

131
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:02,660
Ready for the counter?

132
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:04,250
He's coming, Wakatsuki!

133
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:06,990
...That Kansai-accent one is so loud. Ha.

134
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:11,940
...My analysis before and during the match is almost complete.

135
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:14,500
...Their defense consists of three phases.

136
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:21,630
...Phase one... as soon as their opponent gains possession, Hayate will quickly press.

137
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:28,220
...Phase two... during that, the back four will shift to zone defense.

138
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:31,730
...Forming a wall with no gaps.

139
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,880
If there are no gaps, I'll create one myself!

140
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:37,440
...I'll launch the strongest weapon I have at them!

141
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:44,720
Go, Otoya!

142
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:46,950
Let's break through them, Karasu!

143
00:10:49,450 --> 00:10:52,490
Try your luck, clumsy ninja.

144
00:10:52,490 --> 00:10:55,710
I can hear your light footsteps from a mile away!

145
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,920
...And who said...

146
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,270
I'd infiltrate alone?

147
00:11:00,270 --> 00:11:03,340
Nice! Now speed up and slip behind him!

148
00:11:05,130 --> 00:11:06,230
Not bad, you two.

149
00:11:06,230 --> 00:11:09,560
You and that sharp-tongued one are quite in sync.

150
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:11,790
But we're still equal nonetheless.

151
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:15,600
...And finally... the third phase.

152
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:21,150
...The safety valve that comes in when things get heated... Aiku.

153
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:27,200
These three phases... are the foundation of Japan U-20's defense.

154
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:30,930
How unlucky for you, ninja boy.

155
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:33,160
Idiot.

156
00:11:33,850 --> 00:11:35,330
And who said there are only two of us?

157
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:42,090
...This was our aim from the beginning.

158
00:11:42,430 --> 00:11:46,010
...Go... our third arrow!

159
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:51,620
The fastest runner in all of Blue Lock!

160
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:55,400
Create a gap for us... princess!

161
00:12:02,110 --> 00:12:05,190
...He responded to me in advance...! Just as expected from the captain.

162
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:07,910
...Catch me if you can!

163
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:14,580
...You might be better than me in overall movement across the entire field.

164
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:19,540
...But right now we're on the right wing, and it's just a straight line!

165
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:21,630
...My speed...

166
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:23,470
...will resonate...

167
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:27,630
...all over the world!!!

168
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:31,600
...And the moment...

169
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:37,870
...the moment I've always dreamed of...

170
00:12:39,850 --> 00:12:41,270
...is right in front of me!!!

171
00:12:43,970 --> 00:12:46,820
W-what an incredible speed!!

172
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:52,160
...Blue Lock's number 4, Chigiri Hyoma, has broken through the right side, creating a passing opportunity!!

173
00:12:52,470 --> 00:12:56,050
All Blue Lock players are now charging into the penalty area!!

174
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:00,190
Should I push further in...?

175
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:02,830
...Damn... I have no choice but to pass.

176
00:13:03,190 --> 00:13:04,590
...The one least marked right now is...

177
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:10,080
...As if I'd stay in defense the whole match, idiots!

178
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,220
Karasu...?

179
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:14,290
Great positioning, assassin!

180
00:13:14,290 --> 00:13:15,930
I owe you one!

181
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:19,230
...Pass it to me... Red.

182
00:13:20,190 --> 00:13:22,270
The ball is sent to the least crowded area!

183
00:13:22,270 --> 00:13:23,740
And there's someone free!

184
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:28,490
...A perfect pass, princess...! The ball is barely within my shooting range.

185
00:13:29,050 --> 00:13:30,470
...Thanks.

186
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,260
...Is he serious...?

187
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:39,750
...He read my positioning with extreme precision!

188
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:40,830
Well done, genius!

189
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:41,870
Loose ball!

190
00:13:44,790 --> 00:13:45,580
Rin!

191
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:49,550
Shoot if you're a man!

192
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:53,080
...I underestimated you.

193
00:13:54,150 --> 00:13:58,500
...I thought you were just traditional, useless Japanese players.

194
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:02,010
...Ones who just follow the coaches' plans.

195
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:04,270
...But I was wrong!

196
00:14:05,090 --> 00:14:11,120
...All of you are striving to change your fate with your goals!

197
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,840
...You're starving monsters!

198
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:14,990
Rin!

199
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,950
Interesting.

200
00:14:17,950 --> 00:14:20,450
...So you two are planning to get past me with a two-on-one.

201
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:23,550
...Quick passes...! I read that!

202
00:14:24,490 --> 00:14:26,340
...But it's just a decoy!

203
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,900
I figured it out!

204
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:30,800
...You're right-footed.

205
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:33,590
...And if you shoot with your left,

206
00:14:33,590 --> 00:14:36,800
...the power and accuracy of your shot will drop, just like when you imitated your brother!

207
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,090
...So I'll gladly open up the shooting angle for your left foot.

208
00:14:40,770 --> 00:14:41,650
...But...

209
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,900
...I'll kill your shooting angle with your right foot!

210
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:49,070
...You'll be forced to shoot with your left in this position, so there's nothing to worr-

211
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:12,550
...He shot a curved shot with the outside of his right foot?!

212
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:27,060
...You guys are the best... Blue Lock.

213
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:31,230
Gooooooooooal!!!!

214
00:15:34,770 --> 00:15:40,940
...Japanese football has finally... gotten some new genes!

215
00:15:42,350 --> 00:15:46,940
They've overturned the score to 2-1!!! Who would have predicted such a development in the match?!

216
00:15:46,940 --> 00:15:47,740
You're right!

217
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:50,420
Is he a genius or what?

218
00:15:50,890 --> 00:15:53,280
....From his movement to prevent him from knowing the timing of his shot...

219
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:55,790
...to his shot with the outside of his right foot!

220
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:00,260
...So this is the extent of his abilities when he's serious.

221
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:01,990
Rin!

222
00:16:06,310 --> 00:16:08,900
Five minutes left until the end of the first half.

223
00:16:09,650 --> 00:16:11,360
So we'll use Plan B.

224
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:12,990
Sir, yes, sir!

225
00:16:12,990 --> 00:16:14,290
...You're so annoying.

226
00:16:14,290 --> 00:16:15,830
What matters is we turned the score around.

227
00:16:15,830 --> 00:16:18,260
You were a great decoy, Isagi!

228
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,570
...Damn.

229
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:22,010
I'll score the next goal!

230
00:16:23,070 --> 00:16:24,270
...Those kids.

231
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:25,650
...Damn.

232
00:16:25,650 --> 00:16:27,500
...Damn it!

233
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:30,710
...Sorry, guys... I let him shoot.

234
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:35,600
...It can't be helped if even you couldn't stop him... and it was a two-on-one anyway.

235
00:16:37,110 --> 00:16:40,730
If this indicates anything, it's that he's truly the brother of that genius.

236
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:46,190
How many more chances are you going to waste before you score, you bum dreaming of marrying a model?

237
00:16:46,190 --> 00:16:48,100
Mo-... what?!

238
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:51,450
Things came to this because you didn't score and got the ball stolen from you.

239
00:16:51,990 --> 00:16:55,820
You're the cause of this situation, you lowly forward!

240
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:58,120
Y-you must be joking!

241
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:03,530
...Maybe the ball was stolen from me, but you can't put all the blame on me!

242
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:05,540
...I'm not blaming you.

243
00:17:06,130 --> 00:17:09,870
...This is just something from someone who creates chances for you.

244
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:12,270
Score goals!

245
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:17,280
Or will they take our spots representing the U-20 if we lose?

246
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:22,950
...Well... I don't care either way.

247
00:17:23,820 --> 00:17:25,700
I won't let it end like this!

248
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:28,160
Use me more, Sae-kun!

249
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:29,910
Can I go further forward?

250
00:17:29,910 --> 00:17:32,730
Yeah... ha... Let's equalize before the half ends!

251
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:38,330
So you've finally fired up, you spoiled brats.

252
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:40,830
Let's go, guys!

253
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:47,480
Consider the remaining minutes of the first half as all we have!

254
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:54,540
Only a few minutes left until the end of the first half!

255
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:57,670
No one ever imagined Japan U-20 losing before the match started!

256
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:04,410
Will the Blue Lock team be able to stop Japan U-20's attack and finish the first half in the lead?

257
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:12,600
...They've increased their numbers in attack more than before.

258
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:22,530
...Furthermore, having Itoshi Sae deep makes them use shorter passes to advance.

259
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,530
They're playing more desperately now than before!

260
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,740
Here they come!

261
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,370
Watch the wing!

262
00:18:28,370 --> 00:18:30,580
Got it! I'll handle him!

263
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,540
Come at me, you howling fox!

264
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:36,710
Take this, you buzzing bee!

265
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:38,300
I'm here!

266
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:40,010
...So that was your aim from the beginning.

267
00:18:40,710 --> 00:18:43,500
...You're not the only ones who changed your game plan.

268
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,940
...To protect the lead in the last five minutes,

269
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:51,640
...all of us will drop back to defend except Nagi!

270
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:57,440
This is Plan B, which allows the Blue Lock team, made up entirely of forwards, to win!

271
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,400
Cut it off, Bachira; it's a two-on-one!

272
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:00,780
You don't need to tell me!

273
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,070
Kitsune!

274
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:04,040
U-... use me!

275
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:06,370
You came just in time!

276
00:19:06,370 --> 00:19:08,290
Get them, Chou-kun!

277
00:19:08,990 --> 00:19:11,200
Great. I'll score.

278
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,000
In your dreams!

279
00:19:13,310 --> 00:19:14,870
Nice, Niko!

280
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:22,640
Your sliding challenge narrowed down his options, which made it possible for me to read the course of his shot just as I did!

281
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,820
Great save!

282
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:26,090
Not yet! Loose ball!

283
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:31,520
One minute of added time! Let's get through this at all costs!

284
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:34,100
Damn!

285
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:40,130
Get him!

286
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:41,530
Defend! Stop him!

287
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:44,040
We'll surround him!

288
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:44,860
Here he comes!

289
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:48,870
From that direction?

290
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:50,700
...No!

291
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:53,240
...How fast!

292
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:55,040
He passed between us...?

293
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,000
...How skillful!

294
00:20:04,310 --> 00:20:05,930
...What a terrible cross.

295
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:08,390
...It's impossible for me to reach it.

296
00:20:08,770 --> 00:20:10,600
No! I'll score it!

297
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:13,180
...And become a hero!

298
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:14,390
...How pitiful.

299
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,280
You aim to become the best in the world with a pass like this...?

300
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:21,970
You're dreaming, you filthy brother!

301
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,430
...He did it!

302
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:29,490
...Great!

303
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:32,710
...Don't stand in my way.

304
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:37,750
...What an annoying little brother you are.

305
00:20:53,290 --> 00:20:55,900
I... am being glam!

306
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:58,560
They held on!

307
00:21:15,590 --> 00:21:16,720
Awesome!

308
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:18,290
We managed to hold on!

309
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:20,210
Can you believe this?! 2-1!

310
00:21:20,210 --> 00:21:21,170
This is insane!

311
00:21:21,170 --> 00:21:24,830
Who would have predicted that the first half would end with the Blue Lock team in the lead?!

312
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:05,120
Blue Lock: Additional Time!

313
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:08,780
Is your item ordinary or not?

314
00:23:08,810 --> 00:23:11,210
Let's begin the "Ordinary or Not?" program!

315
00:23:11,210 --> 00:23:12,820
O-o-o-ordinary!

316
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:14,160
And here's our first item!

317
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,950
Whoa! What's this?

318
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:18,580
This is a vase my father gave me.

319
00:23:18,580 --> 00:23:21,790
He said it cost about five million yen. Isn't it wonderful?

320
00:23:21,790 --> 00:23:23,880
What do you say, Karasu-sensei?

321
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:25,910
Ordinary.

322
00:23:25,910 --> 00:23:27,440
Whoa! It's ordinary!

323
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,560
Why?!

324
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:30,380
Let's hear sensei's explanation.

325
00:23:30,730 --> 00:23:34,580
An artwork revolves around whether the artist put their soul into it or not.

326
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:38,190
And this one looks like it was made just for money, which makes it boring.

327
00:23:38,190 --> 00:23:39,430
Therefore, it's ordinary.

328
00:23:39,430 --> 00:23:41,680
Thank you for participating!

329
00:23:39,430 --> 00:23:41,680
...My... five-million-yen vase...

330
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,170
Next up, please!

331
00:23:43,170 --> 00:23:45,730
My name is Igarashi Gurimo, from Aichi Prefecture!

332
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:49,730
This is a precious scroll passed down through generations at the temple my family runs!

333
00:23:49,730 --> 00:23:53,110
...It's very precious to my parents, so I hope that...

334
00:23:53,110 --> 00:23:54,030
Ordinary.

335
00:23:54,660 --> 00:23:57,450
Unfortunately, it's a fake, baldy.

336
00:23:57,450 --> 00:24:01,030
People will think your family is incredibly stupid for not having realized it's a fake until now!

337
00:24:01,030 --> 00:24:04,330
So I advise you to throw it in the nearest trash can immediately, you dimwit!

338
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:06,230
Thank you for participating!

339
00:24:04,790 --> 00:24:08,140
No way!! No!

340
00:24:06,310 --> 00:24:09,500
And now for our final participant!

341
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,040
My name is Bachira Meguru!

342
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:12,950
I brought my treasures!

343
00:24:13,460 --> 00:24:15,630
W-what exactly are these things...?

344
00:24:15,630 --> 00:24:17,490
This is an acorn I picked up while practicing dribbling!

345
00:24:18,210 --> 00:24:22,600
And also there are pretty stones, marbles, and my baby teeth!

346
00:24:22,820 --> 00:24:25,910
...This is my molar, this is my front tooth, and this...

347
00:24:24,520 --> 00:24:26,280
Who would want this?! Gross!

348
00:24:25,910 --> 00:24:28,690
Now it's time for your evaluation, Karasu-sensei!

349
00:24:26,280 --> 00:24:27,690
Isn't this just garbage?

350
00:24:29,810 --> 00:24:30,690
Not ordinary!

351
00:24:30,690 --> 00:24:32,700
Yay! I did it!

352
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:32,710
Whaaaaat?! Why?

353
00:24:32,710 --> 00:24:33,980
How?!

354
00:24:33,980 --> 00:24:35,810
...I see you two still don't understand.

355
00:24:35,810 --> 00:24:39,070
To be not ordinary means to be filled with egoism and originality.

356
00:24:39,310 --> 00:24:42,380
...A passion and an experience that cannot be replicated anywhere in the world.

357
00:24:42,380 --> 00:24:45,210
Pursuing that is what makes you not ordinary.

358
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:48,750
Therefore, there are eight billion not-ordinary people.

359
00:24:48,750 --> 00:24:50,080
See you again next week!

360
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:51,630
O-o-o-ordinary!

361
00:24:51,630 --> 00:24:53,160
And that's the dream I dreamed!

362
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:54,210
Three nights in a row!

363
00:24:54,210 --> 00:24:54,870
Not ordinary!

364
00:24:54,870 --> 00:24:56,090
O-o-o-ordinary!